  "notes": "Prices are list prices captured by clicking every program/size tab on the product pages (2026-10-31). Homepage ran a Halloween '50% OFF' promo (Oct 30–Nov 1) with the code only revealed in Discord, so discount_code=null. CFD Prime 2-Phase not offered at $200K. Headline rule fields = CFD Prime 1-Phase (the widget default). CFD Instant leverage is lower (FX 1:30, indices/commodities 1:7.5); CFD Prime FX 1:50, indices 1:15, commodities 1:10, crypto/stocks 1:2. News: allowed on CFD up to $50K, banned within ±2 min of high-impact news on $100K/$200K; allowed on futures, stocks and CFD Instant. Weekend holding: allowed on CFD Prime; CFD Instant closes commodities/metals/energies/crypto before the weekend; futures and stocks are intraday-only. Futures Prime requires 3 trading days to pass; CFD requires 3 profitable days (≥0.5% each). CFDs not offered to residents of USA, Canada and Russia (homepage disclaimer); futures unavailable in ~29 further countries incl. Russia, Iraq, Belarus (help centre). The countries_restricted list is the full no-service list. Stocks: the product page shows 6% target / 4% max DD / $95 & $225, but the help article says 7% / 5% / €99/$99; the product page values are used. founded=null: their own site gives no year (Trustpilot's company-written blurb says Feb 2022, which is not used per sourcing rules). Majority-owned by Pinorena Capital (Illimar Mattus). Trustpilot: 'rating unavailable due to a breach of our guidelines' with a note that fake reviews were removed; 1,085 reviews, 68% 5-star / 22% 1-star; the latest review (29 Oct 2026) complains about profits removed on consistency grounds. trustpilot=null. Homepage claims $18M+ in rewards and 10,000+ active monthly accounts.",
